  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1242 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nFollowing the passage of Friday's cold front, dry and seasonable\nmild conditions are forecast to open the new week. A weak/dry \nsecondary cold front will pass through the area Sunday morning, \nbut this will only bring a brief increase in high cloud cover. \nHigh pressure centered across the Great Plains will retrograde \ninto the area by the middle of next week, bringing a gradual \ntemperature warm up.\n\nTemperatures through Tuesday will be fairly close to normal \nvalues for early October. However, as the area of high pressure \nand H5 ridging increase, temperatures will warm to around 5-10 \nabove normal for the second half of the week. This pattern will \nalso result in dry conditions for the next week at least, with \nensemble guidance suggestion the region could remain dry for the\nnext 10 days or so.",
